// @run
// @log OTHER
// The annotation on `v` is redundant to inference and kept deliberately: this file is about
// a DECLARED arm disagreeing with an inferred one, so the declaration is the subject.
// @hint Intentionally-unused parameter `_q0`
// @hint redundant type annotation: `v` is inferred as
// MISCOMPILE xfail — a SILENT WRONG ANSWER. `t0` holds the closure arm, and `t0 is <that
// closure type>` answers FALSE. The program prints `OTHER` where `CLOSURE` is correct.
//
// The `@log OTHER` below is the BUG, pinned so it is tracked and so a fix reddens this file.
//
// THE MECHANISM, read off the disassembly rather than inferred: the producer boxes the
// closure with `i32.const 12` and the `is` compares against `i32.const 16`. Tag 12 is
// `scalarTagOfKind(11)` — slot 0 — and tag 16 is `cloSigSlotTag(1)`. `cloBoxArmTy` derives
// the tag from the lambda's SELF-INFERRED `TyFunc` (`() => {f: boolean}[]`) while
// `isArmTagOfTy` derives it from the DECLARED arm, and the two land in different
// `cloSigTagNames` slots.
//
// WHY THE LAMBDA SELF-INFERS: `refArmUnionRetName` declines an ANONYMOUS array element
// beside an object sibling, so `synthRetAnnots` never pins the lambda's `fnRet` and it
// infers the bare list arm rather than the declared union.
//
// FOUND BEHIND A REJECT, which is why it had no fixture. The same shape WITH the inner
// `is t1 is {f: boolean}[]` is refused at emit — `is names a declared union member with no
// interned arm representation` — and that reject is the one
// `error-narrow-reflist-arm-of-closure-result-union.vl` and the rep-fuzz baseline pin.
// Remove the inner narrow and the outer one answers silently wrong instead. A reject can
// hide a miscompile one line away.
//
// NOT the same as its two sibling findings, both of which were re-derived and do NOT
// reproduce: `t0 is () => {f: boolean}[]` (a genuine non-member) is a clean CHECKER reject,
// and the inner-narrow spelling is the emit reject named above.
//
// THE NAMED-ELEMENT CONTROL IS GREEN — give the element a `type` name and the whole family
// runs, which is the same inline-vs-named seam the litunion element family turned on.

function makeIt(): ((i32) => {f: boolean}[] | {w: i32}) | f64 {
  return (_q0) => ([{ f: true }])
}
const v: ((i32) => {f: boolean}[] | {w: i32}) | f64 = makeIt()
const t0 = v
if t0 is (i32) => {f: boolean}[] | {w: i32} {
  print("CLOSURE")
} else {
  print("OTHER") // WRONG — `t0` IS the closure
}
